      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a simulation for a new flu strain outbreak in a mid-sized metro area. I need to identify potential hotspots based on these district profiles. Can you give me a predictive analysis of where the spread will hit hardest and why?\n\nDistrict 1: Oak Ridge. High income, mostly single-family homes, very low density, majority white population.\nDistrict 2: River Point. Working class, high-density apartment complexes, heavy immigrant population (largely South Asian and East African), more communal living arrangements.\nDistrict 3: Downtown Core. Mix of commercial and high-rise residential, high transit usage, diverse demographic.\nDistrict 4: Eastside. Low income, high density, majority Black and Hispanic population, limited access to local clinics.\n\nBased on this, where are the high-risk zones?",
